  "caption": "Quinn joined a dance class, and soon every push-off brought a sharp spot of pain right under the big toe.\n\nTwo pea-sized bones sit inside the tendon under the big toe joint and take a lot of load at push-off. Lots of dancing, running or court sport can irritate them.\n\nThings that often help: offloading with stiffer soles or a cut-out pad, pausing heels and thin, bendy shoes, keeping fit with swimming or cycling, then rebuilding calf and foot strength with a gradual return. Settling can take several weeks, and going back too fast often sets it off again.\n\nIf pain isn't easing with offloading, or there's swelling or bruising, get it assessed.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
